# Code quality

## TypeScript discipline

- Type everything. No `any`. Use `unknown` and narrow.
- Reuse types. Don't redefine the same shape twice — import it.
- Types live in `<Feature>.types.ts` next to the feature, not in a global `types/` dump.
- Form schemas use zod. Derive TS types with `z.infer<typeof schema>` so the schema is the single source of truth.

## File co-location per feature

A feature is a small set of co-located files:

- `Feature.tsx` — the component(s)
- `Feature.types.ts` — types and zod schemas
- `Feature.utils.ts` — pure logic, exported for unit tests
- `Feature.module.scss` — styles

Don't pre-create empty files. Add `.utils.ts` when there's logic worth testing. Add `.types.ts` when there are 2+ shared types. Until then, keep them inline in `Feature.tsx`.

## Pure logic in utils

- Anything that doesn't touch React (transformations, validation, parsing, math, formatting) lives in `.utils.ts`.
- Components import and call. Components don't define logic inline beyond trivial render-time expressions.
- Util functions are pure where possible. Pure = same input, same output, no side effects, unit-testable without mocks.

## Unit tests (required)

Every component and feature module under `apps/web/src/components/` and `apps/web/src/features/` must have tests before merge.

**File pairing:**

| File | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `Feature.utils.ts` | Pure logic (when non-trivial logic exists) |
| `Feature.utils.test.ts` | Utils unit tests — no DOM, fast |
| `Feature.test.tsx` | Component render + interaction smoke tests |

**What to test:**

- **Utils** — happy path, edge cases, and error branches for extracted logic.
- **Components** — renders without crash, key `data-testid` / roles, one primary interaction (click, toggle, submit) when applicable.
- Don't re-test logic already covered in `*.utils.test.ts` inside component tests.

**Infrastructure:** Vitest + happy-dom + Testing Library; use `renderWithProviders` from `src/tests/render.tsx`. Router-dependent components need `withRouter: true` or a minimal route tree (see `MobileNav.test.tsx`).

**When adding or changing a component:** add or update its test files in the same PR. No new component without `Feature.test.tsx`; extract logic to `Feature.utils.ts` + `Feature.utils.test.ts` when the component has non-trivial branching, formatting, or data transforms.

## Don't

- Don't use `any` to silence type errors. Fix the type or use `unknown` and narrow.
- Don't put `fetch` calls in components or utils. They go in services.
- Don't create a util file just to have one. Inline trivial helpers.
- Don't mix zod schemas and unrelated types in the same `.types.ts`. Split if the file grows past ~150 lines.
